        nothing failed:
    
        - strict: ``passed_structured_reference`` only when the frozen reference
          comparison genuinely passed, the required numeric checks (finite and,
          when it was run, convergence) passed and were actually present, and the
          source validation is fully supported; anything less stays
          ``not_verified`` -- unknown provenance is never promoted to pass and
          never auto-failed either.
        - normal mode keeps the original semantics: a numerical pass without a
          reference is only an honesty label, and only a reference fail or a
          numeric failure is a fail.
    
        ``source`` is the ``_source_validation`` mapping (its exact contents are
        not re-read here).
